🤖 Managed Tuning
Your Data → Google manages more → Tuned Model

⚙️ Custom Tuning
Your Data + More Configuration → You control more → Tuned Model

========

Managed Tuning vs Custom Tuning

| Feature                      | 🤖 Managed Tuning                 | ⚙️ Custom Tuning                           |
| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| **Who manages the process?** | Google manages most of it         | You have more control                      |
| **Difficulty**               | Easier                            | More advanced                              |
| **Configuration**            | Simple/basic                      | Detailed configuration                     |
| **Hyperparameters**          | Mostly managed or limited control | More control over settings                 |
| **Best for**                 | Beginners and standard use cases  | Advanced and specialized use cases         |
| **Your work**                | Provide data and requirements     | Provide data + configure training settings |
| **Control**                  | Less                              | More                                       |


=======

🤖 Managed Tuning
Training Examples
       ↓
Google / Vertex AI manages tuning
       ↓
Tuned Model
Example

You give Vertex AI 1,000 business consulting examples:

Input:

How can I increase bakery sales?

Expected Output:

Use WhatsApp marketing, combo offers, and loyalty programs.

You provide the examples, and Vertex AI handles most of the tuning process.

👉 Easy option.

======

⚙️ Custom Tuning
Training Examples
       +
Your Training Settings
       ↓
Custom Tuning
       ↓
Tuned Model

You may have more control over settings such as:

Learning rate
Training steps
Other hyperparameters
Training configuration
Example

Suppose you are building a highly specialized AI for textile manufacturing and have thousands of carefully prepared examples. 
You want to experiment with different training configurations to achieve better performance.

👉 More control, but more advanced.


=========

🎂 Simple Cake Example
Managed Tuning

You tell the baker:

“Make me a chocolate birthday cake.”

The baker handles most of the details.

Custom Tuning

You tell the baker:

“Use these exact ingredients, quantities, temperature, and preparation settings.”

You control many more details.

